      "body": "## What\r\n\r\nOn ROCm, `test_voxtral_realtime_generator` OOMs at startup because the previous test (`test_voxtral_realtime_forward`) never releases its in-process engine. Both build an engine at `gpu_memory_utilization=0.9` in the same pytest process, and pytest keeps the fixture value alive through teardown, so the first engine's VRAM is still held when the second one starts.\r\n\r\n## Fix\r\n\r\nDrop the engine reference in the fixture teardown and reclaim memory via the same helpers `VllmRunner`/`HfRunner` already use (`cleanup_dist_env_and_memory` + `wait_for_rocm_memory_to_settle`). No-op off ROCm.\r\n\r\n## Test\r\n\r\n`pytest tests/models/multimodal/generation/test_voxtral_realtime.py` on MI300X: before `1 passed, 1 error` → after `2 passed`.\r\n\r\n## TODO\r\n\r\n- [ ] Validate on MI325 (`mi325_1`), the original failing job. Same `gfx942` arch, so the fix should carry over, but it hasn't been run there yet.",
